AMT, LLC (AMT) is seeking a highly motivated and diverse Civil Engineer Intern to join the engineering team in our Washington, DC office for the 2027 internship period. This is a paid full-time position with an anticipated duration of May through August 2027 (flexible) and has the potential to transition into a Full-Time Role upon graduation. The successful candidate will work under the supervision of Project Managers and Team leaders, with partnerships with other engineering staff.
Responsibilities
Support various project tasks, including regulatory requirements/reviews, research, procurement support, etc.;
Perform data entry, management, evaluation, and presentation;
Support the preparation of reports, plans, and specifications for clients;
May work on engineering field assignments as needed;
May work on survey field assignments as needed;
Will be supported by leaders, mentors, and teammates;
Perform other related duties and responsibilities as necessary.
Qualifications
Must be at least 18 years old;
Pursuing Bachelor or Associates Degree in Civil/Transportation Engineering or related field;
Minimum GPA of 3.0;
Has excellent verbal and written communication skills;
Possesses solid technical and problem-solving skills;
Self-motivated, detail oriented person;
AutoCAD experience is preferred;
Proficient in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, and Power Point); and
Honest, fun, hard-working and ready to learn and grow.
Why Join AMT?
At AMT, we understand that our most valuable asset is our staff. For 70 years, we have worked diligently to build a team of talented employees who fully embody our values as an organization – values such as teamwork, integrity, and innovation. Now that we have transitioned into an employee-owned firm, we are excited to place the future of AMT into over 500 sets of dedicated hands.
The AMT Difference
Our company culture is characterized by a workforce that holds the highest standards of ethics and integrity, focused client care, and commitment to AMT's Core Values of safety, respect, integrity, commitment, quality, teamwork. leadership, responsibility, and profitable growth.
Operating as an ESOP allows us to reward our dedicated and loyal employees with additional benefits from the company’s stock as well as an incentive to continue building a high-performance ownership culture. To strengthen and support its employees, AMT invests in programs and processes to sustain an engaging work environment. AMT also recognizes the importance of employee benefits and policies and remains committed to providing programs that are both comprehensive and competitive in the industry.
Competitive Benefit Package
To strengthen and support its employees, its greatest asset, AMT invests in programs and processes to sustain an engaging work environment. AMT also recognizes the importance of employee benefits and policies and remains committed to providing programs that are both comprehensive and competitive in the industry. With AMT, you will get:
• Tiered medical coverage
• Dental/Vision
• 401(k) with a generous 6% Company Match
• Short- and long-term disability
• College savings plan
• Life insurance
• Paid time off
• Holidays
• Training/Certifications

A. Morton Thomas and Associates, Inc. (AMT) is seeking a highly motivated Civil Engineering undergraduate student to join us as a Transportation Engineer Intern in our Richmond, Virginia office for the 2027 summer internship period. Candidates should have an interest in Roadway Design, Traffic Engineering or Hydraulic Design. This is a paid, full-time summer internship position with an anticipated duration from Mid-June through mid-August 2027 (flexible dates) and has the potential to transition into a full-time position upon graduation.
Responsibilities
The selected candidate will work under the supervision of Project Managers and Design Team Leaders and may be expected to perform the following tasks:
Prepare roadway, trail and sidewalk design plans using Bentley OpenRoads Designer (ORD) and Microstation design platforms;
Prepare meeting exhibits and construction plans;
Prepare Basis of Design reports and specifications;
Identify potential utility conflicts and avoidance measures;
Calculate quantities and prepare cost estimates;
Conduct site visits and field inspections;
Perform other design and related tasks, as directed
Minimum Requirements
Must be at least 18 years old;
Rising 3rd year or 4th year student pursuing BSCE;
Minimum GPA of 3.0;
Excellent verbal and written communication skills;
Possess solid technical and problem-solving skills;
Self-motivated and detail-oriented;
Ability to work in a fast-paced team environment;
Hard-working and willingness to take direction
Why Join AMT?
